WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.866
During their journey to Laverre City

2
00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:08.966
and Ash's sixth Kalos Gym Badge challenge, our heroes take time for a rest stop.

3
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:12.333
Pikachu, drink lots of water before we head out.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.966
Pika, pika.

5
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.166
It looks like it's gonna be hot again today.

6
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:18.966
- Chespin, Chespin!
- Pancham, Pancham!

7
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.466
Let's see. My fortune for today is...

8
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:26.200
Huh? "Troubles await you?" What does that mean?

9
00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:31.466
- Oh, boy. I wanna know my fortune too.
- Bonnie's fortune today is...

10
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:32.500
There we go.

11
00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:36.066
"Today will be the worst day you've had all year.

12
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.200
You'll be sorry you ever got up this morning.

13
00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:40.600
And watch out for things made of gold."

14
00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:43.533
- Hey. That's bad.
- Now, don't worry.

15
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.733
Fortune-telling is just for entertainment.

16
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.100
Don't give it another thought.

17
00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:50.866
We've got enough food for a small city.

18
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:53.866
Remind me to send that berry tree a thank-you card.

19
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:55.333
We lucked out, all right.

20
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.266
Look out below. Twerp alert.

21
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.200
This is our lucky day.

22
00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:02.633
So why don't we pick up some Pokémon, too?

23
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.833
When fortune smiles on you, you just smile on back.

24
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.233
'Kay, you guys, let's move out.

25
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.066
- Pancham.
- Chespin.

26
00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.266
- You OK?
- Who could've done that?

27
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:19.200
- Why, your favourite raves.
- You did miss us, didn't you?

28
00:01:19.266 --> 00:01:21.666
- Twerps always do.
- Wobba, wobba!

29
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:22.866
Here.

30
00:01:25.366 --> 00:01:26.733
Cham! Cham!

31
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.633
- Chespin.
- Pancham.

32
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.733
Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.

33
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.300
Pikachu!

34
00:01:35.066 --> 00:01:37.133
And our anti-zapper wins.

35
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.433
If that's the case, Luxray, Swift, let's go.

36
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.666
Lux! Luxray!

37
00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:52.433
- Che!
- Pan, pan!

38
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.866
- Pancham.
- Chespin, you're all right.

39
00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.633
What's that?

40
00:01:58.766 --> 00:02:01.700
Hm. It must be theirs.

41
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.700
Pangoro!

42
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:10.233
Criminals. Those berries happen to belong to us.

43
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.333
- Picked fresh today.
- Grab your own grub.

44
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.866
We're not stealing anything.

45
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.500
Pangoro!

46
00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.866
- Pangoro.
- Pangoro!

47
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.800
-Goro! Goro!

48
00:02:25.633 --> 00:02:28.300
Pangoro, calm down, please?

49
00:02:28.366 --> 00:02:30.700
- Run for it! Come on!
- Pika!

50
00:02:31.933 --> 00:02:34.233
Che!

51
00:02:34.366 --> 00:02:36.733
- Goro!
- Pan!

52
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

53
00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:42.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

54
00:02:42.633 --> 00:02:46.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

55
00:02:46.066 --> 00:02:47.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

56
00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:51.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

57
00:02:51.366 --> 00:02:54.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

58
00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:58.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

59
00:02:58.066 --> 00:03:02.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

60
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

61
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

62
00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:14.833
So You're Having a Bad Day!

63
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.333
Aah! Aah!

64
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.333
Huh? It's Meowth.

65
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.333
It's the fun-size twerpette.

66
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.833
Pangoro!

67
00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.933
-Pangoro!

68
00:03:35.433 --> 00:03:36.433
Huh?

69
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.933
-Pan.

70
00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:49.800
That was no fun. Dedenne, are you OK?

71
00:03:49.866 --> 00:03:51.933
Ne! Denne-ne! Ne-ne-ne-ne!

72
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.533
- Where are we?
- Stop pullin' me.

73
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.933
- What's this? Cut it out, will you?
- Whoa! Cool your jets!

74
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.300
It's nothin' but a teensy vine.

75
00:04:01.366 --> 00:04:03.333
And don't sass me, see?

76
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.833
I'm the famous Meowth from Team Rocket.

77
00:04:08.466 --> 00:04:11.266
- Or not.
- You're so useless.

78
00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.833
Pangoro!

79
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.899
- I'm outta here.
- Aah! This way.

80
00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.966
- Aaaah!
- This way.

81
00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:21.966
Pangoro!

82
00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:25.633
Pangoro!

83
00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.000
Cham, cham, cham! Pan, pan!

84
00:04:29.066 --> 00:04:31.933
What was that all about? Everybody OK?

85
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.366
Pan, pan. Cham, cham.

86
00:04:33.433 --> 00:04:37.600
Huh? Everybody? Where'd they go?

87
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.833
Well, I guess we got away.

88
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.033
Huh? Hey, where's Ash?

89
00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.933
- Chespin, che.
- Frogadier.

90
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:51.933
- Luxray.
- Lucha.

91
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.200
- Fletch! Fletch, fletch!
- Ray?

92
00:04:54.266 --> 00:04:56.733
It looks like we've been separated from the others.

93
00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.566
- Pika.
- Let's look around.

94
00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:00.533
Pika.

95
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.600
Wob. Wobba. Wobba.

96
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:06.933
- Meowth's lost again?
- Well, let's get to it.

97
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.500
- Help us look, Inkay.
- That Meowth.

98
00:05:09.566 --> 00:05:12.900
- If it's not one thing, it's another!
- Inkay!

99
00:05:12.966 --> 00:05:16.400
- Aah! Unh! Did it work?
- Not even a scratch.

100
00:05:16.466 --> 00:05:17.800
-Denne-ne.

101
00:05:17.866 --> 00:05:20.500
Guess we're stuck. Here's the deal.

102
00:05:20.566 --> 00:05:23.366
I'm escortin' you back to your twerpie buddies.

103
00:05:23.433 --> 00:05:25.633
- Ah! Oh, really?
- Ah!

104
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.233
You'll take me to your buddies and steal Dedenne.

105
00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.366
I know a lie when I hear one.

106
00:05:30.433 --> 00:05:31.300
Denne-ne.

107
00:05:31.366 --> 00:05:35.200
- I'd never do such a thing.
- It's written all over your face.

108
00:05:35.266 --> 00:05:39.933
My face? This cute mug only has whiskers and no newsprint.

109
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.466
- Is that thing made out of gold?
- Hey. Hey!

110
00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:45.333
I'll have you know that this Charm is part of my charm.

111
00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.333
So keep your paws off of it.

112
00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.666
But why do you have a Charm?

113
00:05:49.733 --> 00:05:51.933
Why? That's a good question.

114
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.233
You sure are a mystery.

115
00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:58.633
- Hey, how come you can talk?
- I'm glad you asked me that.

116
00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:02.433
You see, kid, the story behind that is long and sad.

117
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.700
- But what an ending.
- Never mind.

118
00:06:04.766 --> 00:06:07.233
Eh? But you're the one who asked in the first place..

119
00:06:10.466 --> 00:06:12.733
- What's with the racket?
- I get it.

120
00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.900
My fortune said today was gonna be the worst day ever.

121
00:06:15.966 --> 00:06:18.400
Boy, did they get that right.

122
00:06:18.466 --> 00:06:21.000
- Eh?
- And watch out for gold stuff.

123
00:06:21.066 --> 00:06:24.733
- That thing's made out of gold.
- Hey! That was just plain rude.

124
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:25.633
-Huh?

125
00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.833
- Will you stop pulling on me?
- Aaah!

126
00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:33.766
Hey! Serena! Clemont! Bonnie! Where are you?

127
00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:34.866
Pancham, Pan!

128
00:06:34.933 --> 00:06:39.100
Let's head for higher ground. Maybe that way, we'll see better.

129
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:40.766
Pancham, cham.

130
00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.166
Pika, pi!

131
00:06:44.233 --> 00:06:46.366
Braixen, brai!

132
00:06:46.433 --> 00:06:47.433
Bunnelby.

133
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.500
It's OK. You leave it to me. I know just the thing to do.

134
00:06:51.566 --> 00:06:52.966
Pikachu...

135
00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:58.966
The future is now, thanks to science. Clemontic Gear on.

136
00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:01.666
My Body-Detecting Radarbot, Mark Three.

137
00:07:01.733 --> 00:07:03.766
- Pika!
- Bunnelby.

138
00:07:03.833 --> 00:07:06.800
Also called the Life Detector.

139
00:07:06.866 --> 00:07:08.266
Braixen, brai.

140
00:07:08.333 --> 00:07:11.100
All right. Switch on.

141
00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.766
Onward, my perfect creation.

142
00:07:20.066 --> 00:07:21.733
This is what's called a thermograph.

143
00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.266
A thermograph detects and displays warm bodies,

144
00:07:24.333 --> 00:07:28.000
- in other words, people and Pokémon.
- Pika, pika!

145
00:07:28.066 --> 00:07:32.766
But it can't tell us what it's reacting to, whether it finds people or Pokémon.

146
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:38.533
This thermograph shows us, so... Wait. Something's coming this way.

147
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.833
- It just might be Ash.
- Pika!

148
00:07:41.933 --> 00:07:43.566
Pangoro!

149
00:07:43.633 --> 00:07:44.633
Pangoro!

150
00:07:45.366 --> 00:07:47.533
- Pango!
- Braix!

151
00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.233
Pangoro!

152
00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.233
Now's our chance to escape.

153
00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.733
- Braixen, brai.
- Pika!

154
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.500
- Braixen, you saved us. Thanks.
- Braixen.

155
00:07:58.566 --> 00:08:02.466
Hey, Ash. Clemont. Bonnie!

156
00:08:02.533 --> 00:08:05.466
- They're not here.
- Pin, pin, che.

157
00:08:05.533 --> 00:08:08.466
- Gadier.
- Oh, Frogadier, do you see something?

158
00:08:08.533 --> 00:08:09.833
Frog, frog.

159
00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.400
- Gadier.
- Right.

160
00:08:13.466 --> 00:08:17.133
You're so sweet to be acting as my bodyguard, Frogadier.

161
00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.233
- Thank you.
- Chespin.

162
00:08:21.366 --> 00:08:24.000
- Chespin.
- Heh. You too, Chespin?

163
00:08:24.066 --> 00:08:26.400
- Do you wanna be my bodyguard?
- Chespin.

164
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:32.633
- Gadier.
- Chespin, che. Che.

165
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.866
- Pangoro.
- Che!

166
00:08:33.933 --> 00:08:35.533
- Che! Chespin!
- Pan!

167
00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.766
Che, che, che! Chespin! Che! Che!

168
00:08:37.833 --> 00:08:39.100
Oh, Chespin.

169
00:08:39.166 --> 00:08:41.166
Pangoro!

170
00:08:41.233 --> 00:08:43.433
Frogadier!

171
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.833
- Goro, goro!
- Frogadier.

172
00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.533
Thanks a lot. Che!

173
00:08:50.566 --> 00:08:54.466
- I'm starvin'.
- Me too.

174
00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.300
-Denne-ne.

175
00:08:59.866 --> 00:09:01.533
Wow.

176
00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.266
- And up, and up, and up.
- Good luck, Meowth.

177
00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.700
Hm.

178
00:09:08.766 --> 00:09:12.333
Oh, uh... Cool!

179
00:09:14.266 --> 00:09:17.200
Mm!

180
00:09:17.266 --> 00:09:21.000
Hey. You were supposed to share with us.

181
00:09:21.066 --> 00:09:22.500
Nope. I picked it.

182
00:09:22.566 --> 00:09:23.700
- Mm-mm!
- Mm...

183
00:09:23.766 --> 00:09:25.533
- Denne-ne. Denne.
- Huh?

184
00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:28.700
- You're gonna get us some food?
- Denne!

185
00:09:28.766 --> 00:09:31.200
Ne-ne-ne, ne-ne-ne!

186
00:09:31.266 --> 00:09:33.666
Ne-ne-ne-ne! Ne!

187
00:09:33.733 --> 00:09:37.166
- Ne! Denne.
- Hm. I've got it. Thanks a lot.

188
00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.000
Ne-ne-ne. Denne-ne!

189
00:09:41.066 --> 00:09:45.700
- Ah! Nice shot. Thanks, pal.
- Nope. You didn't get this one.

190
00:09:45.766 --> 00:09:49.166
- So this is mine.
- No fair. You've got two.

191
00:09:49.233 --> 00:09:52.033
Well, you didn't share with me before, did you?

192
00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:55.800
Hey. Fine! If you wanna be that way. Good luck!

193
00:09:55.866 --> 00:09:58.433
I am not gonna move an inch from this spot.

194
00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.633
Let's see you find those twerps now.

195
00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.166
- Say that again.
- I'm not movin'.

196
00:10:03.233 --> 00:10:07.700
Hm. Dedenne. Use Nuzzle.

197
00:10:07.766 --> 00:10:11.833
Denne. Nenne, ne-ne-ne-ne-ne-ne-ne!

198
00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.833
Denne!

199
00:10:17.533 --> 00:10:20.500
Denne-ne. Denne-ne! Nenne!

200
00:10:20.566 --> 00:10:23.900
Bickerin' at a time like this isn't good for our health.

201
00:10:23.966 --> 00:10:27.333
You're right. In that case...

202
00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.833
- Here.
- Thanks. Down the hatch.

203
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.433
- Mm. Yummy stuff.
- Mm. Yeah. It sure is.

204
00:10:33.866 --> 00:10:36.000
Denne-ne. Nenne.

205
00:10:36.066 --> 00:10:38.833
Who's that Pokémon?

206
00:10:43.066 --> 00:10:45.633
It's Pangoro.

207
00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.266
Pangoro.

208
00:10:51.533 --> 00:10:52.700
Inkay, ink.

209
00:10:52.766 --> 00:10:56.266
- Did you locate Meowth?
- Inkay.

210
00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.300
- Or the twerps and their Pokémon?
- Pumpka.

211
00:11:01.366 --> 00:11:04.166
Hm. We're out of "lucked out".

212
00:11:04.233 --> 00:11:06.300
Wobba, wobba.

213
00:11:09.066 --> 00:11:12.633
Whoa! Wow, what a view! I can see everything!

214
00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:16.666
- Pancham!
- Cool. I thought so. Hey, Fletchinder.

215
00:11:16.733 --> 00:11:20.466
- Pancham! Pancham!
- Fletch! Fletchinder!

216
00:11:20.533 --> 00:11:23.533
- Fletch! Fletchinder!
- Lucha!

217
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.700
Hey, you guys. So where have you been?

218
00:11:25.766 --> 00:11:26.766
Chinder, fletch!

219
00:11:26.833 --> 00:11:29.800
Fletchinder? Will you look for all the others from the air?

220
00:11:29.866 --> 00:11:31.766
- We'll look too.
- Fletchinder, fle.

221
00:11:32.966 --> 00:11:34.633
-Che!

222
00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.000
- Ah! Luxray.
- Luxray.

223
00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:43.300
Lucha.

224
00:11:43.366 --> 00:11:46.166
- Serena.
- Pancham, Ash.

225
00:11:47.333 --> 00:11:50.833
- You're safe.
- Hey. Is everybody doing all right?

226
00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:51.800
- Froga!
- Che!

227
00:11:51.866 --> 00:11:54.800
Frogadier made sure we all stayed safe.

228
00:11:54.866 --> 00:11:57.100
- Good job.
- Froga.

229
00:11:57.166 --> 00:12:01.333
- Hey, Ash, where's Braixen?
- I don't know. We haven't found it yet.

230
00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.866
And I still don't know where Clemont, Bonnie, and Pikachu are.

231
00:12:08.566 --> 00:12:11.600
- Goro.
- Shh.

232
00:12:11.733 --> 00:12:14.866
Goro. Goro.

233
00:12:19.933 --> 00:12:22.100
Goro.

234
00:12:22.166 --> 00:12:23.400
Aah.

235
00:12:23.466 --> 00:12:25.500
-Goro.

236
00:12:25.566 --> 00:12:27.566
Pangoro?

237
00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.666
Huh? Aaargh!

238
00:12:31.733 --> 00:12:34.666
Foongus! Foongus!

239
00:12:34.733 --> 00:12:38.833
Huh? Uh-oh. This isn't good.

240
00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.433
Oh, man. Hang in there, twerpette.

241
00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.300
- Denne-ne.
- Hm.

242
00:12:44.366 --> 00:12:47.200
She must've gotten a giant-sized whiff of Spore.

243
00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:49.533
We've gotta get some Chesto Berries, and fast.

244
00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.800
Denne.

245
00:12:50.866 --> 00:12:53.600
Dedenne, can you find some Chesto Berries?

246
00:12:53.666 --> 00:12:54.633
Denne-ne-ne.

247
00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.200
You can't? Shorty doesn't know what they look like.

248
00:12:57.266 --> 00:13:01.266
Now what am I gonna do? I'm kind of tied up.

249
00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:05.433
- All right. Here we go.
- Ne.

250
00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:06.700
She's heavy.

251
00:13:06.766 --> 00:13:07.700
-Denne-ne!

252
00:13:07.766 --> 00:13:12.700
One... two... three... four...

253
00:13:12.766 --> 00:13:18.433
Ugh! She's like bricks. This Pokémon's got guts.

254
00:13:19.166 --> 00:13:22.933
My guts are bustin'.

255
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.933
I've gotta keep goin'!

256
00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.300
Keep... going...

257
00:13:28.366 --> 00:13:30.500
going... gone...

258
00:13:30.566 --> 00:13:32.833
I've gotta work out more often.

259
00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.066
Denne.

260
00:13:35.466 --> 00:13:38.566
Dedenne, you're gonna have to get some of those Chesto Berries

261
00:13:38.633 --> 00:13:40.033
by hook or by crook.

262
00:13:41.666 --> 00:13:43.633
Dig it. Chesto Berries look like this.

263
00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.100
Denne-ne!

264
00:13:45.233 --> 00:13:49.000
Ne-ne-ne-ne! Denne! Ne!

265
00:13:49.066 --> 00:13:51.100
Denne-ne. Ne.

266
00:13:51.166 --> 00:13:52.166
Denne.

267
00:13:53.133 --> 00:13:56.166
Denne-ne! Ne-ne-ne-ne-nenne-nenne!

268
00:13:56.233 --> 00:13:57.900
Ne-ne-ne-ne-ne!

269
00:13:58.633 --> 00:14:01.000
Denne! Ne...

270
00:14:01.066 --> 00:14:03.000
- Ne-ne-ne-ne-ne?
- Huh?

271
00:14:03.066 --> 00:14:05.400
- Ne, ne.
- Bingo. That's the one.

272
00:14:05.466 --> 00:14:08.733
You're pretty smart to find one of those things right away.

273
00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:12.466
- Denne-ne!
- Here, down the hatch.

274
00:14:15.433 --> 00:14:18.833
- Denne-nenne.
- All we do is wait for her to come to.

275
00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:22.733
Mm... Yucky!

276
00:14:24.133 --> 00:14:25.833
Hey, what happened?

277
00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:29.900
You got a heapin' helpin' of Spore and took a trip to Dreamy Land.

278
00:14:29.966 --> 00:14:32.533
But Dedenne found some Chesto Berries fast.

279
00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.266
- And here we are.
- That's what happened?

280
00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:38.500
- Wow, Dedenne, thanks.
- Denne-ne!

281
00:14:38.566 --> 00:14:41.566
- Let's get back to lookin' for the gang.
- OK.

282
00:14:42.266 --> 00:14:43.300
- Huh?
- Pika.

283
00:14:43.366 --> 00:14:47.866
Fletchinder. Hey. Fletchinder.

284
00:14:47.933 --> 00:14:51.033
- Clemont?
- Ash, Serena.

285
00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.000
- Pika, pi! Pikachu!
- Pikachu.

286
00:14:54.066 --> 00:14:57.233
- Braixen. I'm glad you're safe.
- Braixen.

287
00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.533
- Uh, where's Bonnie?
- Huh? She's not with you?

288
00:15:06.633 --> 00:15:09.000
- What a klutz.
- Aah!

289
00:15:18.866 --> 00:15:22.000
- Up there.
- Grab it.

290
00:15:22.066 --> 00:15:24.033
That was close!

291
00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.966
My clothes are soaking wet.

292
00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.733
- Dedenne? Are you feeling all right?
- Denne-ne-ne.

293
00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.900
- Come on. Ah!
- Sorry about that.

294
00:15:34.966 --> 00:15:37.500
- Hey, look. The vine got cut in two.
- Huh?

295
00:15:37.566 --> 00:15:39.400
- You're right.
- Denne-ne!

296
00:15:39.466 --> 00:15:42.200
Which means we can go our separate ways.

297
00:15:42.266 --> 00:15:44.533
Woo-hoo. Yay, what a relief.

298
00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:47.000
Ready, Dedenne? Let's get going.

299
00:15:47.066 --> 00:15:48.166
Denne-ne!

300
00:15:49.166 --> 00:15:54.600
It's about time. You know, I've had just about enough twerpette for one day.

301
00:15:54.666 --> 00:15:56.866
Even if I am totally alone.

302
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.933
Pangoro!

303
00:16:00.066 --> 00:16:04.633
Did you hear that? I wonder if that scary Pangoro's close.

304
00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.266
- Denne-ne.
- Hold the phone.

305
00:16:06.333 --> 00:16:08.033
- Hey, wait a sec!
- Now what?

306
00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.700
- I thought you had enough of me.
- Aw.

307
00:16:10.766 --> 00:16:14.800
Well, since I've already come this far, I might as well get you back

308
00:16:14.866 --> 00:16:16.933
to your twerpy pals safe and sound.

309
00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.733
Really?

310
00:16:22.866 --> 00:16:24.933
Course, if I run into that Pangoro,

311
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.033
I'll use these dumbbells as a distraction and get away.

312
00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:34.666
- Huh? It's Fletchinder.
- The twerps must be close.

313
00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.933
- Fletchinder!
- Bonnie! Bonnie!

314
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.066
-Pika, pika!

315
00:16:39.133 --> 00:16:42.733
- Finally. Bonnie. Are you OK?
- Hm.

316
00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.400
And I'm sure glad to see you're OK too.

317
00:16:45.466 --> 00:16:48.600
- All of us are feeling just fine.
- What's going on?

318
00:16:48.666 --> 00:16:53.200
- Why is Meowth with you?
- You see, it's kind of a long story.

319
00:16:53.266 --> 00:16:56.333
Anyway, I'm glad to see you back with your buds.

320
00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.800
Pangoro!

321
00:16:59.866 --> 00:17:02.566
- Pangoro again.
- Wow. They don't give up.

322
00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.333
Pan!

323
00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.633
Cham! Pancham, cham!

324
00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.599
Pancham. Cham, pan.

325
00:17:08.666 --> 00:17:11.966
- Pan, Pangoro.
- Pancham, cham.

326
00:17:12.033 --> 00:17:15.066
Meowth, come on. You know what they're saying.

327
00:17:15.133 --> 00:17:18.900
- So tell us right now.
- Don't push me. All right!

328
00:17:19.033 --> 00:17:21.433
Goro. Pangoro-o.

329
00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:24.866
I guess they're havin' a problem with their food supply.

330
00:17:24.933 --> 00:17:26.333
Their food supply?

331
00:17:29.033 --> 00:17:30.833
See... that's their tree.

332
00:17:30.966 --> 00:17:33.166
Pangoro, Pangoro!

333
00:17:33.233 --> 00:17:35.966
Pangoro says this tree grows gobs of grub.

334
00:17:36.033 --> 00:17:39.666
So every year, they get together and divide up that grub between them.

335
00:17:39.733 --> 00:17:42.500
- Goro, Pangoro.
- So all of a sudden they see some crooks

336
00:17:42.566 --> 00:17:45.366
who steal all their berries and then run away...

337
00:17:45.433 --> 00:17:48.366
- So. You mean...
- It was you, huh?

338
00:17:48.433 --> 00:17:49.733
Shh.

339
00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.866
- So you're the cause of all this.
- Hey, I didn't know.

340
00:17:52.933 --> 00:17:55.066
Tough break. What can we say?

341
00:17:55.133 --> 00:17:57.500
Maybe you could just tell them you're really sorry.

342
00:17:57.566 --> 00:17:58.766
Pikachu.

343
00:17:58.833 --> 00:18:00.600
Pangoro. Pan, pan.

344
00:18:00.666 --> 00:18:04.733
They saw you holdin' their grub, so they thought you twerps took it.

345
00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.000
We just picked up the berries where we found them.

346
00:18:08.066 --> 00:18:12.066
- The real bad guys are Team Rocket.
- Hey, no fair. Don't bust me.

347
00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.366
Pan, pan. Goro.

348
00:18:14.433 --> 00:18:17.100
You know, I've asked myself the same thing.

349
00:18:17.166 --> 00:18:18.933
- Good question. Aah!
- There you are.

350
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.900
- We've been searching everywhere.
- Look. Three Pangoro.

351
00:18:22.966 --> 00:18:24.933
- Wob!
- Why'd ya have to show up now?

352
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.633
Prepare for trouble, it's now or never!

353
00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.933
And make it double. We're all together!

354
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.733
Well, this time that's not a good thing!

355
00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.333
To protect the world from devastation!

356
00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.933
To unite all people within our nation!

357
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:40.100
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

358
00:18:40.166 --> 00:18:43.266
To extend our reach to the stars above!

359
00:18:43.333 --> 00:18:45.833
- Jessie!
- And James.

360
00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:48.666
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

361
00:18:48.733 --> 00:18:51.933
Surrender now or prepare for a reunification fight!

362
00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.300
Meowth, that's right!

363
00:18:53.366 --> 00:18:54.366
Wobbuffet!

364
00:18:56.833 --> 00:18:59.666
Oopsie. Guess the catchy lyrics dragged me in.

365
00:19:01.333 --> 00:19:02.733
- 'Scuse me?
- Dragged into what?

366
00:19:04.033 --> 00:19:07.033
Pangoro!

367
00:19:10.633 --> 00:19:11.766
- Huh?
- Bad move.

368
00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:17.566
Now that they know it was us, they're not too pleased.

369
00:19:17.633 --> 00:19:21.166
- Not pleased? What does that mean?
- That sounds dangerous.

370
00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:23.766
Pangoro!

371
00:19:25.533 --> 00:19:28.833
- Our motto caused this?
- Long story.

372
00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.733
We're blasting off again!

373
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:34.766
- Now.
- Pika. pika

374
00:19:34.833 --> 00:19:37.700
- Here are your berries.
- That's all of them.

375
00:19:37.766 --> 00:19:39.966
Yup. Now you've got them all back.

376
00:19:40.866 --> 00:19:44.033
- Pangoro.
- Pangoro-ro.

377
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:50.100
- So dig in. Huh? For me?
- Awesome. Thanks a lot.

378
00:19:50.166 --> 00:19:54.100
- I think they're sorry. This is so nice.
- It sure is.

379
00:19:54.166 --> 00:19:57.400
-All right, we know just what to do.

380
00:20:00.166 --> 00:20:02.433
Let's eat. Mm!

381
00:20:03.433 --> 00:20:05.200
That's good.

382
00:20:05.866 --> 00:20:07.666
Pangoro.

383
00:20:07.733 --> 00:20:11.266
- See you later, Pangoro.
- Be well, everybody.

384
00:20:11.333 --> 00:20:14.866
- Thanks for the food.
- Bye-bye.

385
00:20:17.133 --> 00:20:20.300
Tied to Meowth with a vine? That sounds awful.

386
00:20:20.366 --> 00:20:23.233
Your fortune said you'd have the worst day of the year.

387
00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.033
It wasn't all that bad. Actually, it was fun.

388
00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.300
Even with Meowth. Right, Dedenne?

389
00:20:29.366 --> 00:20:30.500
Denne-ne.

390
00:20:30.566 --> 00:20:32.500
- You're kidding.
- Huh?

391
00:20:32.566 --> 00:20:34.466
Pika.

392
00:20:34.533 --> 00:20:38.300
Although our heroes and their Pokémon were separated,

393
00:20:38.366 --> 00:20:41.100
they all managed to find each other again.

394
00:20:41.166 --> 00:20:43.700
Perhaps that was in their fortune too.

395
00:20:43.766 --> 00:20:48.300
But one thing's for sure. Their journey continues.
